# AI Router product description

AI Router is a service for unified access to generative AI models from external providers without the need to deploy infrastructure. It allows you to work with [available models](#available-models) through a single interface, centrally manage access keys and quotas, and receive combined reporting and analytics on their usage.

If you need unified access to models deployed on Selectel infrastructure, use [Token Factory](/token-factory/).

Terms of use for the AI Router product are determined by the document [Terms of use of individual services: "AI Router"](https://files.selectel.ru/docs/ru/conditions-ai-router.pdf) and SLA.

## Tasks solved \{#tasks-to-be-solved}

* connecting OpenAI, Anthropic, and other models via a single API key;
* using a single codebase for each OpenAI-compatible provider;
* paying for models from a single balance instead of separate accounts with each provider;
* setting budget limits;
* monitoring consumption through detailed real-time analytics.

## How it works \{#principle-of-operation}

AI Router acts as a universal gateway between your application and external model providers. The service sends requests via an OpenAI-compatible API to connected [models](#available-models), for details see the [official OpenAI Developers documentation](https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/overview). At the same time, you do not need to configure integrations with each provider separately — it is enough to use the AI Router API key in requests.

## How to work with AI Router \{#manage-ai-router}

To get started, create an AI Router; for details, see the [AI Router: Quickstart](/ai-router/quickstart.mdx) instructions.

After creating an AI Router, you can:

* manage the AI Router in the [Control panel](https://my.selectel.ru/ml/default/ai-router):

  * [manage API keys](/ai-router/manage/manage-api-keys.mdx);
  * [view consumption](/ai-router/manage/get-consumption.mdx) and [metrics](/ai-router/manage/view-metrics.mdx) of the AI Router;
* configure [request masking](/ai-router/manage/data-masking.mdx) to hide sensitive data;
* use AI Router to work with [available models](#available-models) via the API.

## Available models \{#available-models}

You can view the current list of models with prices at [selectel.ru](https://selectel.ru/prices/), as well as after creating an AI Router in the [Control panel](https://my.selectel.ru/ml/default/ai-router): in the top menu, click **Products** → **AI Router** → AI Router page → the **Models** tab.

## Areas of responsibility \{#areas-of-responsibility}

### Selectel provides \{#selectel-provides}

* access to models via a public API compatible with the OpenAI API;
* a monitoring system for AI Routers in the Control panel;
* consumption analytics;
* the ability to manage limits for each AI Router and API key;
* technical support.

### Selectel is not responsible for \{#selectel-is-not-responsible}

* the functionality of requests executed with API keys and request results;
* the processing of personal data within the service;
* integrating models into your projects;
* the business logic of model operation in your projects.

Protecting API keys from compromise is your responsibility.

## Cost \{#price}

AI Router is billed according to the [pay-as-you-go](/balance-and-payments/payment-models.mdx#pay-as-you-go) model. Funds are deducted from the balance every hour for the model consumption volume during the previous hour; for details, see the [Payment model and AI Router prices](/ai-router/about/payment.mdx) instructions.

### What is included in the cost \{#what-included-in-price}

An unlimited number of tokens for using [available models](#available-models).

## Limitations \{#limitations}

AI Router does not support:

* training AI models;
* uploading custom models to the catalog;
* deploying models from the catalog On-Premises, in an A-DC, on dedicated servers, and in a certified cloud.

