# Token Factory product overview

:::info

The product is in private preview.

:::

Token Factory is a service for unified access to generative AI models within the Selectel environment without the need to deploy infrastructure. It allows you to work with [available models](#available-models) through a single interface with pay-per-token billing, centrally manage access keys, and receive overall reporting and analytics on their usage.

Token Factory provides access only to models deployed on Selectel infrastructure. If you need access to models from external providers, use [AI Router](/ai-router/).

Token Factory supports [projects](/access-control/projects/about-projects.mdx).

## Tasks solved \{#tasks-to-be-solved}

* connecting models via a single public OpenAI-compatible API key;
* paying for models from a single balance;
* monitoring consumption via detailed real-time analytics.

## How it works \{#principle-of-operation}

Token Factory acts as a universal gateway between your application and [models](#available-models) deployed on Selectel infrastructure. The service sends requests to models using an OpenAI-compatible API; for details, see the [official OpenAI Developers documentation](https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/overview). You do not need to configure integrations with each model separately — simply use the Token Factory API key in your requests.

## How to work with Token Factory \{#manage-token-factory}

To get started, submit a request to test Token Factory; for details, see the [Token Factory: Quickstart](/token-factory/quickstart.mdx) instructions.

After gaining access to Token Factory, you can:

* manage Token Factory in the [Control panel](https://my.selectel.ru/ml/default/token-factory):

  * [manage API keys](/token-factory/manage/manage-api-keys.mdx);
  * [view Token Factory usage statistics](/token-factory/manage/view-statistics.mdx);

* use Token Factory to work with [available models](#available-models) via API.

## Available models \{#available-models}

You can view the up-to-date list of models, their specifications, and token prices in the [Control panel](https://my.selectel.ru/ml/default/token-factory): in the top menu, click **Products** → **Token Factory** → **Model Catalog** tab.

## Areas of responsibility \{#areas-of-responsibility}

### Selectel provides \{#selectel-provides}

* access to models via a public OpenAI-compatible API;
* the Token Factory monitoring system in the Control panel;
* consumption analytics;
* ability to manage API keys;
* technical support.

### Selectel is not responsible for \{#selectel-disclamer}

* the content and use of model responses;
* the operability of requests made with API keys;
* personal data processing within the service;
* integrating models into your projects;
* the business logic of model operation in your projects.

Protecting API keys from compromise is your responsibility.

## Cost \{#cost}

Token Factory is paid according to the [pay-as-you-go](/balance-and-payments/payment-models.mdx#pay-as-you-go) model. Funds for tokens consumed in the previous hour are deducted from the balance every hour; for details, see the [Token Factory Billing Model and Prices](/token-factory/about/payment.mdx) instructions.

## Limits and restrictions \{#limits-and-limitations}

In a single [project](/access-control/projects/about-projects.mdx), you can create up to ten API keys.

Token Factory does not support:

* access to AI models from external providers;
* model training capability;
* uploading custom models to the catalog;
* deploying models from the catalog on-premises, in A-DC, on dedicated servers, or in a certified cloud.

